#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sigmond-link — know when a scheduled link (South Pole satellite passes) is down.

The South Pole reaches the outside world only during satellite passes, and
USAP publishes them in advance.  A station that knows the schedule does not
have to find each gap by timing out: the uploader holds, the fetch timers
skip, and the backlog ships when the next pass opens.
See tasks/plan-constrained-link-delivery.md (Phase 4).

  sigmond-link fetch [--force]
      the timer's mode (every 15 min).  Refreshes the schedule when it is
      older than refresh_hours, and ONLY while the link is up by the current
      schedule (or there is none): a fetch in a gap is exactly the attempt
      this tool exists to prevent.  Disabled: removes the schedule file, and
      every consumer stops gating.
  sigmond-link status [--json]
      up/down now, the reason, the next change, the next windows
  sigmond-link gate
      exit 0 = go ahead, 1 = the link is down by schedule.  Used as
      ExecCondition= by the units in gated_units, so systemd skips their run
      cleanly (no failure) during a gap
  sigmond-link apply
      write or remove the ExecCondition drop-ins for gated_units
  sigmond-link tick   (alias: rac)
      the every-minute timer: the gateway probe, then the RAC guard.
  sigmond-link probe [--now]
      the probe alone (--now ignores probe_min); prints what answered

The probe (every probe_min minutes, ALWAYS, in a pass or a gap): ONE tcp
connect to each gateway in turn until one answers — vpn1/vpn2 at a HamSCI
station, gw1/gw2 at a wsprdaemon-RAC one.  An answer is proof the link is up,
whatever the schedule says: it opens a "probe window" in the schedule file
lasting probe_min * probe_fail_count + 1 minutes from the answer, and each
further answer extends it.  The gated units, hs-uploader's LinkGate and the
RAC guard all read that file, so all of them go ahead while the gateways
answer, and the schedule's gap comes back on its own probe_fail_count rounds
after they stop.  The probe can only OPEN the link in schedule mode, never
close it, so a gateway outage cannot gag a station whose link is fine.
  mode = "probe" drops the schedule entirely: the link is up while the probe
answers and down after probe_fail_count rounds without an answer.  It also
fails open: no targets, or the tick stopping, lets everything run within
probe_min * (probe_fail_count + 1) minutes.
  probe_min = 0 never sends a probe (a site whose IT objects to them); the
schedule alone then decides, and RAC keeps its dead man and ceiling.
  Targets: probe_targets, else the gateways this machine's frpc configs name,
else DEFAULT_PROBE_TARGETS (both HamSCI and both wsprdaemon gateways; a guest
VM has no frpc config of its own).  Results: /var/lib/sigmond/link-probe.json.

The RAC guard (the second half of every tick).  In a scheduled gap it stops the
      remote-access tunnels (frpc retries every few seconds otherwise) and
      starts them again when the next pass opens.  Remote access is how
      these stations are supported, so a schedule error must never cost it
      for long.  Four nets, any one of which brings RAC back:
        1. a dead man: at suspension, a transient systemd timer is armed to
           start the tunnels at the gap's end (capped at max_suspend_hours),
           so the restart does not depend on this tool surviving
        2. the probe (above): while a gateway answers, the link is up
           whatever the schedule says, so RAC runs
        3. a ceiling: suspended for max_suspend_hours, RAC runs regardless for
           rac_resume_hold_min, then the schedule may suspend it again
        4. fail open: disabled, no/stale/bad schedule, or any error in the
           tick starts every tunnel it knows of

The schedule file, read by hs-uploader's LinkGate and by `gate`:
  /var/lib/sigmond/link-schedule.json
  {"version": 1, "fetched_at": ISO, "source": ..., "horizon": [ISO, ISO],
   "windows": [{"start": ISO, "end": ISO, "sats": [...]}, ...]}   (all UTC)

Trust the schedule's "no", verify its "yes": inside a window everything runs
and finds out for itself whether the link works.  Fail open: no file, a bad
file, a stale file (fetched more than max_age_days ago) or `now` outside the
horizon all read as "go ahead".  A schedule must never become a gag.

topology.toml (or, on a Proxmox host, which has none, /etc/sigmond/link.toml):
  [link_schedule]
  enabled       = false        # true at a site with a scheduled link
  source        = "usap"       # the USAP weekly PDF (TDRS + DSCS + Skynet),
                               # cross-checked against cel.txt; or the URL of
                               # a windows.json in the format above
  satellites    = "all"        # or a list, e.g. ["TDRS-6"]
  margin_min    = 0            # trimmed off both ends of every pass
  refresh_hours = 6
  max_age_days  = 8
  gated_units   = [...]        # default DEFAULT_GATED below
  rac_suspend   = true         # the RAC guard; false leaves the tunnels alone
  rac_units     = [...]        # default DEFAULT_RAC_UNITS below (globs)
  mode          = "schedule"   # or "probe": no schedule, the probe decides
  probe_min     = 5            # 0 = never probe (was rac_probe_min)
  probe_targets = []           # ["host:port", ...]; [] = auto, see above
  probe_fail_count = 2         # unanswered rounds before a probe window closes
  max_suspend_hours   = 6
  rac_resume_hold_min = 30

On a Proxmox host, /etc/sigmond/link.toml with `follow_vm = <vmid>` (top
level) takes the VM's own [link_schedule] through the guest agent, re-read
hourly and kept in /var/lib/sigmond/link-vm.toml (delete it to re-read now;
after a failed read the copy is used for 5 min before the next try).  The
host keeps its own gated_units, rac_units and probe_targets, and the VM can
lower max_suspend_hours on the host but never raise it above the host's
(default 6).  No answer and no copy: disabled, tunnels run.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import datetime as dt
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path

# tomllib is Python 3.11+.  These helpers run under the system python3 (they
# are symlinked into /usr/local/sbin, not re-exec'd into the venv like smd),
# which is 3.10 on Ubuntu 22.04: fall back to tomli (apt python3-tomli).
try:
    import tomllib
except ModuleNotFoundError:  # py<3.11
    try:
        import tomli as tomllib  # type: ignore[no-redef]
    except ModuleNotFoundError:
        tomllib = None  # type: ignore[assignment]  # callers treat config as absent

TOPOLOGY = Path("/etc/sigmond/topology.toml")
SCHEDULE = Path("/var/lib/sigmond/link-schedule.json")
HOST_CONF = Path("/etc/sigmond/link.toml")
RAC_STATE = Path("/var/lib/sigmond/link-rac.json")
PROBE_STATE = Path("/var/lib/sigmond/link-probe.json")
DEADMAN = "sigmond-link-rac-resume"
DROPIN_NAME = "50-sigmond-link.conf"
SYSTEMD_DIR = Path("/etc/systemd/system")
SELF = "/usr/local/sbin/sigmond-link"

USAP_INDEX = "https://www.usap.gov/technology/1935/"
USAP_BASE = "https://www.usap.gov"
USAP_CEL = "https://www.usap.gov/technology/documents/cel.txt"
UA = "sigmond-link/1 (HamSCI station; South Pole schedule)"
UTC = dt.timezone.utc

# Units whose whole job is to reach the internet, so a run in a gap can only
# time out.  The uploader is not here: hs-uploader reads the schedule itself
# and holds per pipeline.
DEFAULT_GATED = [
    "sigmond-component-fetch.service",      # git fetch of every component
    "apt-daily.service",                    # package lists
    "apt-daily-upgrade.service",            # unattended upgrades
    "hamsci-physics-ionex-download.service",
    "timestd-events.service",               # ships event windows
]

# The remote-access tunnels: the host's per-gateway frpc, and the guest's.
DEFAULT_RAC_UNITS = ["sigmond-rac-host@*.service", "sigmond-rac-host.service", "wd-rac.service"]

# When this machine has no frpc config (a guest VM: its host owns the tunnels),
# probe these in order; any answer means the link is up.  The frps TLS port.
DEFAULT_PROBE_TARGETS = ["vpn1.hamsci.org:35736", "vpn2.hamsci.org:35736",
                         "gw2.wsprdaemon.org:35736", "gw1.wsprdaemon.org:35736"]


def _log(msg: str) -> None:
    # once: under systemd both streams land in the journal
    out = sys.stderr if msg.startswith(("ERROR", "WARNING")) else sys.stdout
    print(f"sigmond-link: {msg}", file=out, flush=True)


def now() -> dt.datetime:
    return dt.datetime.now(UTC).replace(microsecond=0)


def fmt(t: dt.datetime | None) -> str:
    if t is None:
        return "-"
    return f"{t:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M}Z ({t.astimezone():%H:%M %Z})"


VM_CACHE = Path("/var/lib/sigmond/link-vm.toml")
HOST_ONLY_KEYS = ("gated_units", "rac_units", "probe_targets")
# The VM may lower these on the host, never raise them (final review 2026-11-14:
# a typo in the VM must not keep the host's tunnels down for days).
HOST_CEILINGS = {"max_suspend_hours": 6.0}
VM_RETRY_S = 300          # after a failed read, the cached copy for this long
VM_REFRESH_S = 3600       # a good copy is re-read after this long


def vm_link_schedule(vmid: int, run=subprocess.run, cache: Path = VM_CACHE,
                     now: float | None = None, refresh_s: float = VM_REFRESH_S) -> dict | None:
    """The VM's [link_schedule] table, read through the guest agent and kept in
    ``cache`` (the VM's whole topology.toml); the cached copy when the VM or its
    agent is down or answers with bad TOML; None when there is neither.  An
    absent table means disabled ({})."""
    import time
    now = time.time() if now is None else now

    def from_text(text):
        return tomllib.loads(text).get("link_schedule") or {}

    failed = cache.with_name(f".{cache.name}.failed")

    def fresh(p, within):
        try:
            return p.exists() and 0 <= now - p.stat().st_mtime < within
        except OSError:
            return False
    try:
        if fresh(cache, refresh_s):
            return from_text(cache.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    if fresh(failed, VM_RETRY_S):
        try:
            return from_text(cache.read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return None
    try:
        p = run(["qm", "guest", "exec", str(int(vmid)), "--timeout", "15", "--",
                 "cat", "/etc/sigmond/topology.toml"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
        if p.returncode != 0:
            raise OSError((p.stderr or "").strip() or f"qm exited {p.returncode}")
        res = json.loads(p.stdout)
        if int(res.get("exitcode", 1)) != 0:
            raise OSError(f"cat exited {res.get('exitcode')} in VM {vmid}")
        text = res.get("out-data", "")
        table = from_text(text)                      # raises on bad TOML: keep the cache
        cache.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        tmp = cache.with_name(f".{cache.name}.new.{os.getpid()}")
        tmp.write_text(text)
        os.chmod(tmp, 0o644)
        os.replace(tmp, cache)
        failed.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        return table
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 -- fail open: never block on the VM
        try:
            failed.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            failed.touch()
            os.utime(failed, (now, now))
        except OSError:
            pass
        _log(f"following VM {vmid}: cannot read its topology.toml ({type(e).__name__}: {e}); "
             f"using the cached copy" if cache.exists() else
             f"following VM {vmid}: cannot read its topology.toml ({type(e).__name__}: {e}) "
             f"and no cached copy; link schedule disabled")
    try:
        return from_text(cache.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def read_settings(path: Path | None = None, run=subprocess.run, cache: Path = VM_CACHE,
                  now: float | None = None, refresh_s: float = VM_REFRESH_S) -> dict:
    cfg = {"enabled": False, "source": "usap", "satellites": "all", "margin_min": 0.0,
           "refresh_hours": 6.0, "max_age_days": 8.0, "gated_units": list(DEFAULT_GATED),
           "rac_suspend": True, "rac_units": list(DEFAULT_RAC_UNITS),
           "max_suspend_hours": 6.0, "rac_resume_hold_min": 30.0,
           "mode": "schedule", "probe_min": 5.0, "probe_targets": [], "probe_fail_count": 2.0}
    ls = None
    follow = None
    for p in ([path] if path else [TOPOLOGY, HOST_CONF]):
        try:
            with p.open("rb") as fh:
                doc = tomllib.load(fh)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            continue
        ls = doc.get("link_schedule")
        # follow_vm belongs at the top, but a line appended below the table
        # lands inside it; take it there too (final review 2026-11-14).
        follow = doc.get("follow_vm", (ls or {}).get("follow_vm"))
        if ls is not None or follow is not None:
            break
    if follow is not None:
        # A Proxmox host follows its VM (plan 2026-11-14): the VM's table, with
        # the host's own host-only keys (its units and probe targets).
        host = ls or {}
        ls = dict(vm_link_schedule(int(follow), run, cache, now, refresh_s) or {})
        for k in HOST_ONLY_KEYS:
            ls.pop(k, None)                  # never the VM's units or targets
            if k in host:
                ls[k] = host[k]
        for k, dflt in HOST_CEILINGS.items():
            cap = float(host.get(k, dflt))
            ls[k] = min(float(ls.get(k, cap)), cap)
        cfg["followed_vm"] = int(follow)
    if not ls:
        return cfg
    for k in ("enabled", "rac_suspend"):
        if k in ls:
            cfg[k] = bool(ls[k])
    for k in ("source", "satellites", "mode"):
        if k in ls:
            cfg[k] = ls[k]
    if "rac_probe_min" in ls and "probe_min" not in ls:
        cfg["probe_min"] = float(ls["rac_probe_min"])      # the old name
    for k in ("margin_min", "refresh_hours", "max_age_days", "probe_min",
              "max_suspend_hours", "rac_resume_hold_min", "probe_fail_count"):
        if k in ls:
            cfg[k] = float(ls[k])
    for k in ("gated_units", "rac_units", "probe_targets"):
        if k in ls:
            cfg[k] = [str(u) for u in ls[k]]
    if cfg["mode"] not in ("schedule", "probe"):
        raise ValueError(f"[link_schedule] mode must be \"schedule\" or \"probe\", not {cfg['mode']!r}")
    return cfg


# ─── the USAP schedule ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

MONTHS = {m: i for i, m in enumerate("Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep Oct Nov Dec".split(), 1)}
TOK = re.compile(
    r"(?P<nopass>No Pass)"
    r"|(?:(?P<mon>[A-Z][a-z]{2}) (?P<day>\d{1,2}), +)?(?P<h>\d{1,2}):(?P<m>\d{2}) (?P<ap>[AP]M)"
    r"|(?P<dur>\b\d{1,2}:\d{2}\b)")
ROW = re.compile(r"^\s*(\d{2})/(\d{2})/(\d{2})\s+(.*)$")
HDR = re.compile(r"(\S+) Pass (\d)")


def _tok_time(day: dt.date, t: re.Match) -> dt.datetime:
    d = day
    if t.group("mon"):
        mon = MONTHS[t.group("mon")]
        d = dt.date(day.year + (1 if mon < day.month else 0), mon, int(t.group("day")))
    h = int(t.group("h")) % 12 + (12 if t.group("ap") == "PM" else 0)
    return dt.datetime(d.year, d.month, d.day, h, int(t.group("m")), tzinfo=UTC)


def parse_spsat(text: str) -> tuple[dict, list]:
    """The UTC table of the weekly PDF, as `pdftotext -layout` renders it.

    -> ({"YYYY-MM-DD": [[sat, start, end], ...]}, [problems]).  The PDF has
    one table per timezone; only the one headed "(UTC)" is read.
    """
    m = re.search(r"Satellite Schedule \(UTC\)(.*?)(Satellite Schedule \(|\Z)", text, re.S)
    if not m:
        raise ValueError("no UTC table in the schedule PDF")
    slots, rows, problems = None, {}, []
    for line in m.group(1).splitlines():
        if slots is None and "Pass 1" in line:
            slots = [s for s, _ in HDR.findall(line)]
            continue
        r = ROW.match(line)
        if not r or slots is None:
            continue
        mm, dd, yy, rest = r.groups()
        day = dt.date(2000 + int(yy), int(mm), int(dd))
        toks = list(TOK.finditer(rest))
        i, passes, ok = 0, [], True
        for sat in slots:
            if i >= len(toks):
                ok = False
                break
            t = toks[i]
            if t.group("nopass"):
                i += 1
            elif t.group("h") and i + 1 < len(toks) and toks[i + 1].group("h"):
                s, e = _tok_time(day, toks[i]), _tok_time(day, toks[i + 1])
                if e <= s:
                    e += dt.timedelta(days=1)
                passes.append([sat, s.isoformat(), e.isoformat()])
                i += 2
                if i < len(toks) and toks[i].group("dur"):
                    i += 1          # the pass's own duration
            else:
                ok = False
                break
            if i < len(toks) and toks[i].group("dur"):
                i += 1              # a "Total" column
        if not ok or i != len(toks):
            problems.append(f"{day}: unparsed row: {rest.strip()}")
            continue
        rows[day.isoformat()] = passes
    if not rows:
        raise ValueError("the UTC table had no parseable rows")
    return rows, problems


def parse_cel(text: str) -> list:
    """cel.txt: 'MS Y TDS 26/315/144000 191000 043000 ...' — YY/DDD/HHMMSS, UTC."""
    out = []
    for m in re.finditer(r"TDS (\d{2})/(\d{3})/(\d{6}) (\d{6}) (\d{6})", text):
        yy, doy, st, en, _ = m.groups()
        base = dt.datetime(2000 + int(yy), 1, 1, tzinfo=UTC) + dt.timedelta(days=int(doy) - 1)
        s = base + dt.timedelta(hours=int(st[:2]), minutes=int(st[2:4]), seconds=int(st[4:]))
        e = base + dt.timedelta(hours=int(en[:2]), minutes=int(en[2:4]), seconds=int(en[4:]))
        if e <= s:
            e += dt.timedelta(days=1)
        out.append((s.isoformat(), e.isoformat()))
    return out


def cross_check(rows: dict, cel: list) -> tuple[int, int]:
    """(agree, differ) between the PDF's TDRS passes and cel.txt, over the
    days both cover.  Both are UTC; zero agreement means a parser or
    timezone error, which would invert every gap."""
    pdf = {(s, e) for p in rows.values() for sat, s, e in p if sat.upper().startswith("TDRS")}
    cel = set(cel)
    if not pdf or not cel:
        return 0, 0
    lo = max(min(pdf)[0], min(cel)[0])
    hi = min(max(pdf)[0], max(cel)[0])
    a = {p for p in pdf if lo <= p[0] <= hi}
    b = {p for p in cel if lo <= p[0] <= hi}
    return len(a & b), len(a ^ b)


def build(rows: dict, satellites, margin_min: float) -> dict:
    """Rows -> the schedule document's horizon and merged windows."""
    pick = None
    if isinstance(satellites, str) and satellites.lower() != "all":
        satellites = [s.strip() for s in satellites.split(",")]
    if isinstance(satellites, list):
        pick = {s.lower() for s in satellites}
    margin = dt.timedelta(minutes=margin_min)
    raw = []
    for passes in rows.values():
        for sat, s, e in passes:
            if pick and sat.lower() not in pick:
                continue
            s, e = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(s) + margin, dt.datetime.fromisoformat(e) - margin
            if e > s:
                raw.append((s, e, sat))
    raw.sort()
    merged: list = []
    for s, e, sat in raw:
        if merged and s <= merged[-1][1]:
            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], e)
            if sat not in merged[-1][2]:
                merged[-1][2].append(sat)
        else:
            merged.append([s, e, [sat]])
    days = sorted(rows)
    h0 = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(days[0]).replace(tzinfo=UTC)
    h1 = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(days[-1]).replace(tzinfo=UTC) + dt.timedelta(days=1)
    return {"horizon": [h0.isoformat(), h1.isoformat()],
            "windows": [{"start": s.isoformat(), "end": e.isoformat(), "sats": x}
                        for s, e, x in merged]}


def http_get(url: str, binary: bool = False):
    req = urllib.request.Request(url.replace(" ", "%20"), headers={"User-Agent": UA})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=60) as r:
        data = r.read()
    return data if binary else data.decode("utf-8", "replace")


def fetch_usap(old_rows: dict) -> tuple[dict, list]:
    if not shutil.which("pdftotext"):
        raise RuntimeError("pdftotext not installed (apt install poppler-utils)")
    index = http_get(USAP_INDEX)
    links = sorted(set(re.findall(r'href="(/technology/documents/SPSAT[^"?]*\.pdf)', index)))
    if not links:
        raise RuntimeError("no SPSAT pdf linked from " + USAP_INDEX)
    rows, notes = dict(old_rows), []
    for link in links[-2:]:
        pdf = http_get(USAP_BASE + link, binary=True)
        txt = subprocess.run(["pdftotext", "-layout", "-", "-"], input=pdf,
                             capture_output=True, check=True).stdout.decode()
        new, problems = parse_spsat(txt)
        rows.update(new)        # the newer issue wins for the days it covers
        notes.append(f"{os.path.basename(link)}: {len(new)} days")
        notes += problems
    try:
        agree, differ = cross_check(rows, parse_cel(http_get(USAP_CEL)))
        if agree == 0:
            raise RuntimeError("no TDRS pass agrees between the PDF and cel.txt: "
                               "refusing a schedule that may be in the wrong timezone")
        notes.append(f"cel.txt cross-check: {agree} TDRS passes agree, {differ} differ")
    except RuntimeError:
        raise
    except Exception as e:
        notes.append(f"cel.txt cross-check skipped: {e}")
    cutoff = (now() - dt.timedelta(days=21)).date().isoformat()
    return {d: p for d, p in rows.items() if d >= cutoff}, notes


# ─── reading the schedule (the same rules as hs-uploader's LinkGate) ─────────

def load(path: Path | None = None) -> dict | None:
    path = path or SCHEDULE
    try:
        doc = json.loads(path.read_text())
        return doc if isinstance(doc, dict) else None
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None             # missing or corrupt: no schedule; the next fetch replaces it


def evaluate(doc: dict | None, t: dt.datetime, max_age_days: float = 8.0) -> dict:
    """-> {"up": bool, "scheduled": bool, "reason": str, "until": ISO|None}"""
    def r(up, sch, why, until=None):
        return {"up": up, "scheduled": sch, "reason": why,
                "until": until.isoformat() if until else None}
    if doc is None:
        return r(True, False, "no schedule")
    try:
        fetched = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(doc["fetched_at"])
        if fetched.tzinfo is None:
            raise ValueError("naive fetched_at")
        if (t - fetched).total_seconds() > max_age_days * 86400:
            return r(True, False, f"schedule stale (fetched {fmt(fetched)})")
        h0, h1 = (dt.datetime.fromisoformat(x) for x in doc["horizon"])
        if not (h0 <= t < h1):
            return r(True, False, "no schedule covers now")
        for w in sorted(doc["windows"], key=lambda w: w["start"]):
            s, e = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["start"]), dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["end"])
            if s <= t < e:
                sats = w.get("sats", [])
                why = ("gateway answered (" + ", ".join(x[6:] for x in sats if x.startswith("probe:")) + ")"
                       if sats and all(x.startswith("probe:") for x in sats)
                       else "pass " + "+".join(sats))
                return r(True, True, why, e)
            if s > t:
                return r(False, True, "between passes", s)
        if doc.get("source") == "probe":
            return r(False, True, "no gateway answers the probe", h1)
        return r(False, True, "after the last pass", h1)
    except Exception as e:
        return r(True, False, f"schedule unreadable ({type(e).__name__}: {e})")


# ─── commands ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def save(doc: dict, path: Path | None = None) -> None:
    path = path or SCHEDULE
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(doc, indent=1))
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def merge_windows(wins: list) -> list:
    """Overlapping or touching windows -> one, their sats joined."""
    out: list = []
    for w in sorted(wins, key=lambda w: w["start"]):
        s, e = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["start"]), dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["end"])
        if out and s <= out[-1][1]:
            out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)
            out[-1][2] += [x for x in w.get("sats", []) if x not in out[-1][2]]
        else:
            out.append([s, e, list(w.get("sats", []))])
    return [{"start": s.isoformat(), "end": e.isoformat(), "sats": x} for s, e, x in out]


def compose(doc: dict) -> dict:
    """"windows" — what every reader obeys — is the schedule's own windows
    plus the probe's.  The schedule's are kept apart in "sched_windows"."""
    if "sched_windows" not in doc:
        doc["sched_windows"] = doc.get("windows", [])
    doc["windows"] = merge_windows(doc["sched_windows"] + doc.get("probe_windows", []))
    return doc


def cmd_fetch(cfg: dict, force: bool) -> int:
    if cfg["enabled"] and cfg["mode"] == "probe":
        return 0                # no schedule to fetch: the probe writes the file
    if not cfg["enabled"]:
        if SCHEDULE.exists():
            SCHEDULE.unlink()
            _log("disabled: removed the schedule; nothing gates any more")
        return 0
    old = load()
    t = now()
    if old and not force:
        try:
            age = (t - dt.datetime.fromisoformat(old["fetched_at"])).total_seconds()
        except Exception:
            age = 1e12
        if age < cfg["refresh_hours"] * 3600:
            return 0
        st = evaluate(old, t, cfg["max_age_days"])
        if not st["up"]:
            return 0            # a gap: do not try; the next pass refreshes it
    try:
        if cfg["source"] == "usap":
            rows, notes = fetch_usap((old or {}).get("rows", {}))
            doc = {"version": 1, "source": "usap", "rows": rows,
                   **build(rows, cfg["satellites"], cfg["margin_min"])}
        else:
            got = json.loads(http_get(cfg["source"]))
            notes = [f"{cfg['source']}: {len(got['windows'])} windows"]
            doc = {"version": 1, "source": cfg["source"],
                   "horizon": got["horizon"], "windows": got["windows"]}
        doc["fetched_at"] = t.isoformat()
        doc["notes"] = notes
        doc["sched_windows"] = doc["windows"]
        doc["probe_windows"] = (old or {}).get("probe_windows", [])
        compose(doc)
        evaluate(doc, t)        # never write a file the readers cannot read
        save(doc)
        _log(f"schedule refreshed: {len(doc['windows'])} windows, "
             f"{doc['horizon'][0][:10]} .. {doc['horizon'][1][:10]}; " + "; ".join(notes[:4]))
        return 0
    except Exception as e:
        _log(f"WARNING: schedule fetch failed, keeping the old one: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
        return 1


def cmd_status(cfg: dict, as_json: bool) -> int:
    doc = load() if cfg["enabled"] else None
    t = now()
    st = evaluate(doc, t, cfg["max_age_days"])
    nxt = []
    if doc and st["scheduled"]:
        for w in doc["windows"]:
            if dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["end"]) > t:
                nxt.append(w)
            if len(nxt) >= 4:
                break
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"enabled": cfg["enabled"], "now": t.isoformat(), **st,
                          "fetched_at": (doc or {}).get("fetched_at"),
                          "next_windows": nxt}, indent=1))
        return 0
    print(f"link schedule  {'enabled' if cfg['enabled'] else 'disabled'} (source {cfg['source']})"
          + (f", following VM {cfg['followed_vm']}" if cfg.get("followed_vm") else ""))
    if cfg.get("followed_vm"):
        try:
            got = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(VM_CACHE.stat().st_mtime, UTC).replace(microsecond=0)
            print(f"VM {cfg['followed_vm']} copy     read {fmt(got)}; re-read hourly "
                  f"(delete {VM_CACHE} to re-read now)")
        except OSError:
            print(f"VM {cfg['followed_vm']} copy     none yet (the VM has not answered)")
    print(f"now            {fmt(t)}")
    print(f"link           {'UP' if st['up'] else 'DOWN'}  ({st['reason']})")
    if st["until"]:
        u = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(st["until"])
        mins = int((u - t).total_seconds() // 60)
        print(f"changes        {fmt(u)}  in {mins // 60}h{mins % 60:02d}m")
    if doc:
        print(f"fetched        {fmt(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(doc['fetched_at']))}")
        for n in doc.get("notes", [])[:6]:
            print(f"               {n}")
    for w in nxt:
        s, e = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["start"]), dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["end"])
        print(f"  pass  {fmt(s)} -> {fmt(e)}  {'+'.join(w.get('sats', []))}")
    ps = _jload(PROBE_STATE)
    if not cfg["enabled"] or cfg["probe_min"] <= 0:
        print("probe          off" + ("" if cfg["enabled"] else " (link schedule disabled)"))
    else:
        tg = ps.get("targets") or [f"{h}:{p}" for h, p in gateway_targets(cfg)]
        print(f"probe          every {cfg['probe_min']:g} min, mode {cfg['mode']}: {', '.join(tg)}")
        if ps.get("last_probe"):
            lp = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(ps["last_probe"])
            print(f"               last {fmt(lp)}: "
                  + (f"{ps['last_hit']} answered" if ps.get("last_hit") else "no answer")
                  + (f"; {'reachable' if ps.get('reachable') else 'unreachable'} since "
                     f"{fmt(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(ps['since']))}" if ps.get("since") else ""))
            h = ps.get("history", [])
            day = [x for x in h if dt.datetime.fromisoformat(x[0]) > t - dt.timedelta(hours=24)]
            if day:
                print(f"               last 24 h: {sum(1 for x in day if x[1])}/{len(day)} rounds answered")
    rs = _rac_load()
    if rs.get("suspended"):
        print(f"RAC            SUSPENDED since {fmt(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(rs['since']))}: "
              f"{' '.join(rs.get('units', []))}")
    elif rs.get("hold_until"):
        print(f"RAC            running until {fmt(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(rs['hold_until']))} "
              f"({rs.get('hold_why')})")
    else:
        print(f"RAC            {'guarded' if cfg['enabled'] and cfg['rac_suspend'] else 'not guarded'}, running")
    return 0


def cmd_gate(cfg: dict) -> int:
    if not cfg["enabled"]:
        return 0
    st = evaluate(load(), now(), cfg["max_age_days"])
    if not st["up"]:
        _log(f"link down by schedule ({st['reason']}) until {st['until']}: skipping")
        return 1
    return 0


def dropin_text() -> str:
    return ("# Written by sigmond-link apply: skip this run while the link is down by\n"
            "# schedule (South Pole satellite gap).  Exit 1 skips cleanly; it is not a failure.\n"
            f"[Service]\nExecCondition={SELF} gate\n")


def cmd_apply(cfg: dict, root: Path = SYSTEMD_DIR) -> int:
    wanted = set(cfg["gated_units"]) if cfg["enabled"] else set()
    changed = False
    for d in root.glob(f"*.d/{DROPIN_NAME}"):
        unit = d.parent.name[:-2]
        if unit not in wanted:
            d.unlink()
            changed = True
            _log(f"removed the gate from {unit}")
    for unit in sorted(wanted):
        p = root / f"{unit}.d" / DROPIN_NAME
        if p.exists() and p.read_text() == dropin_text():
            continue
        p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        p.write_text(dropin_text())
        changed = True
        _log(f"gated {unit}")
    if changed and root == SYSTEMD_DIR:
        subprocess.run(["systemctl", "daemon-reload"], check=False)
    return 0


# ─── the RAC guard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _systemctl(*args: str) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    return subprocess.run(["systemctl", *args], capture_output=True, text=True)


def rac_units(cfg: dict) -> list:
    """Loaded tunnel units matching rac_units -> [(unit, active)]."""
    out = _systemctl("list-units", "--type=service", "--all", "--no-legend", "--plain",
                     *cfg["rac_units"]).stdout
    res = []
    for line in out.splitlines():
        f = line.split()
        if len(f) >= 3 and f[0].endswith(".service") and f[1] == "loaded":
            res.append((f[0], f[2] == "active"))
    return res


def frpc_gateways(confdir: Path = Path("/etc/sigmond")) -> list:
    """(host, port) of every gateway this machine's frpc configs name."""
    targets = []
    for conf in sorted(confdir.glob("frpc*.toml")):
        try:
            txt = conf.read_text()
            host = re.search(r'^\s*serverAddr\s*=\s*"([^"]+)"', txt, re.M).group(1)
            port = int(re.search(r"^\s*serverPort\s*=\s*(\d+)", txt, re.M).group(1))
        except Exception:
            continue
        if (host, port) not in targets:
            targets.append((host, port))
    return targets


def _hostport(x: str) -> tuple:
    host, _, port = x.strip().rpartition(":")
    return host.strip("[]"), int(port)


def gateway_targets(cfg: dict) -> list:
    """probe_targets, else this machine's frpc gateways, else the defaults."""
    if cfg["probe_targets"]:
        return [_hostport(x) for x in cfg["probe_targets"]]
    return frpc_gateways() or [_hostport(x) for x in DEFAULT_PROBE_TARGETS]


def tcp_probe(host: str, port: int, timeout: float = 8.0) -> bool:
    """One connection attempt; a completed handshake means the link is up."""
    import socket
    try:
        with socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=timeout):
            return True
    except OSError:
        return False


# ─── the gateway probe ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _jload(path: Path) -> dict:
    try:
        d = json.loads(path.read_text())
        return d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def _jsave(path: Path, d: dict) -> None:
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(d, indent=1))
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def probe_tick(cfg: dict, t: dt.datetime | None = None, probe=None, force: bool = False) -> dict:
    """Probe the gateways if a round is due, and keep the probe windows in
    the schedule file.  -> the probe state."""
    t = t or now()
    probe = probe or tcp_probe
    ps = _jload(PROBE_STATE)
    on = cfg["enabled"] and cfg["probe_min"] > 0
    if not on:
        doc = load()
        if doc and doc.get("probe_windows"):
            doc["probe_windows"] = []
            save(compose(doc))
        if cfg["enabled"] and cfg["mode"] == "probe" and SCHEDULE.exists():
            SCHEDULE.unlink()          # probe mode without a probe: fail open
        return ps
    period = dt.timedelta(minutes=cfg["probe_min"])
    last = ps.get("last_probe")
    if not force and last and t - dt.datetime.fromisoformat(last) < period - dt.timedelta(seconds=20):
        return ps

    targets = gateway_targets(cfg)
    hit = None
    for h, port in targets:
        if probe(h, port):
            hit = f"{h}:{port}"
            break
    ps["last_probe"] = t.isoformat()
    ps["targets"] = [f"{h}:{port}" for h, port in targets]
    ps["last_hit"] = hit
    if hit:
        ps["last_answer"] = t.isoformat()
    hist = ps.get("history", [])
    hist.append([t.isoformat(), hit])
    ps["history"] = hist[-300:]                     # ~25 h at 5 min
    was = ps.get("reachable")
    ps["reachable"] = bool(hit)
    if was is None or was != bool(hit):
        ps["since"] = t.isoformat()
        if targets:
            _log(f"gateways {'reachable: ' + hit if hit else 'unreachable: ' + ', '.join(ps['targets'])}")
    _jsave(PROBE_STATE, ps)

    hold = period * cfg["probe_fail_count"] + dt.timedelta(minutes=1)
    doc = load()
    if cfg["mode"] == "probe":
        if not targets:
            if SCHEDULE.exists():
                SCHEDULE.unlink()
            _log("WARNING: probe mode with no gateway to probe: nothing gates")
            return ps
        doc = doc if doc and doc.get("source") == "probe" else {"version": 1, "source": "probe"}
        doc["fetched_at"] = t.isoformat()
        # the horizon ends soon after the next rounds: if the tick stops, the
        # file stops covering `now` and every reader fails open
        doc["horizon"] = [(t - dt.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat(),
                          (t + period * (cfg["probe_fail_count"] + 1)).isoformat()]
        doc["sched_windows"] = []
    elif doc is None:
        return ps                       # no schedule: nothing is gated anyway
    pw = [w for w in doc.get("probe_windows", [])
          if dt.datetime.fromisoformat(w["end"]) > t - dt.timedelta(days=1)]
    if hit:
        end, tag = t + hold, f"probe:{hit}"
        if pw and dt.datetime.fromisoformat(pw[-1]["end"]) >= t:
            pw[-1]["end"] = max(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(pw[-1]["end"]), end).isoformat()
            if tag not in pw[-1]["sats"]:
                pw[-1]["sats"].append(tag)
        else:
            pw.append({"start": t.isoformat(), "end": end.isoformat(), "sats": [tag]})
    doc["probe_windows"] = pw
    save(compose(doc))
    return ps


def _rac_load() -> dict:
    try:
        d = json.loads(RAC_STATE.read_text())
        return d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def _rac_save(d: dict) -> None:
    RAC_STATE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = RAC_STATE.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(d, indent=1))
    os.replace(tmp, RAC_STATE)


def _arm_deadman(units: list, seconds: float) -> bool:
    """A transient systemd timer that starts the tunnels in `seconds`, whatever
    becomes of this tool.  Replaces any earlier one."""
    _systemctl("stop", f"{DEADMAN}.timer")
    _systemctl("reset-failed", f"{DEADMAN}.service")
    r = subprocess.run(["systemd-run", f"--unit={DEADMAN}", f"--on-active={int(seconds)}s",
                        "--timer-property=AccuracySec=5s",
                        "--description=sigmond-link: restart remote access at the end of a gap",
                        "/usr/bin/systemctl", "start", *units], capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode == 0


def _rac_resume(state: dict, why: str) -> None:
    units = state.get("units") or []
    if units:
        _systemctl("start", *units)
    _systemctl("stop", f"{DEADMAN}.timer")
    _log(f"RAC resumed ({why}): {' '.join(units) or '-'}")
    state.update(suspended=False, units=[], since=None)


def rac_tick(cfg: dict, t: dt.datetime | None = None) -> int:
    t = t or now()
    state = _rac_load()
    hold = state.get("hold_until")
    hold = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(hold) if hold else None
    if hold and hold <= t:
        state.pop("hold_until", None)
        state.pop("hold_why", None)
        hold = None
    st = (evaluate(load(), t, cfg["max_age_days"])
          if cfg["enabled"] and cfg["rac_suspend"] else {"up": True, "reason": "guard off"})
    if st["up"] or hold:
        if state.get("suspended"):
            _rac_resume(state, state.get("hold_why") if hold else st["reason"])
        _rac_save(state)
        return 0

    max_s = cfg["max_suspend_hours"] * 3600
    until = (dt.datetime.fromisoformat(st["until"]) if st.get("until") and cfg["mode"] == "schedule"
             else t + dt.timedelta(seconds=max_s))
    if not state.get("suspended"):
        units = [u for u, active in rac_units(cfg) if active]
        if not units:
            return 0
        armed = _arm_deadman(units, min((until - t).total_seconds(), max_s) + 60)
        if not armed:
            _log("WARNING: could not arm the dead-man restart; leaving RAC running")
            return 0
        _systemctl("stop", *units)
        state.update(suspended=True, since=t.isoformat(), units=units)
        _log(f"RAC suspended ({st['reason']}) until {fmt(until)}: {' '.join(units)}")
        _rac_save(state)
        return 0

    since = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(state["since"])
    if (t - since).total_seconds() >= max_s:
        state.update(hold_until=(t + dt.timedelta(minutes=cfg["rac_resume_hold_min"])).isoformat(),
                     hold_why=f"suspended {cfg['max_suspend_hours']:g} h: trying regardless")
        _log(f"WARNING: RAC suspended for {cfg['max_suspend_hours']:g} h; "
             f"running it for {cfg['rac_resume_hold_min']:g} min whatever the schedule says")
        _rac_resume(state, state["hold_why"])
        _rac_save(state)
        return 0
    _rac_save(state)
    return 0


def cmd_rac(cfg: dict, probe: bool = True) -> int:
    if probe:
        try:
            probe_tick(cfg)
        except Exception as e:      # a probe fault must not cost RAC its guard tick
            _log(f"WARNING: probe fault: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
    try:
        return rac_tick(cfg)
    except Exception as e:  # fail open: every tunnel we know of starts
        _log(f"WARNING: RAC guard fault, starting the tunnels: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
        try:
            units = [u for u, _ in rac_units(cfg)] + _rac_load().get("units", [])
            if units:
                _systemctl("start", *sorted(set(units)))
            RAC_STATE.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        except Exception:
            pass
        return 0


def main(argv=None) -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="sigmond-link", description=__doc__.split("\n")[0])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    f = sub.add_parser("fetch")
    f.add_argument("--force", action="store_true")
    s = sub.add_parser("status")
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sub.add_parser("gate")
    sub.add_parser("apply")
    sub.add_parser("rac", help="alias of tick")
    sub.add_parser("tick")
    pr = sub.add_parser("probe")
    pr.add_argument("--now", action="store_true", help="ignore probe_min")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    try:
        cfg = read_settings()
    except Exception as e:
        _log(f"WARNING: cannot read {TOPOLOGY} ({e}); treating the link schedule as disabled")
        cfg = read_settings(Path("/nonexistent"))     # defaults: disabled
        if a.cmd not in ("gate", "rac", "tick"):
            return 1
    if a.cmd == "fetch":
        return cmd_fetch(cfg, a.force)
    if a.cmd == "gate":
        try:
            return cmd_gate(cfg)
        except Exception as e:  # a crash must read "go ahead", never "skip"
            _log(f"WARNING: gate fault, letting the unit run: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
            return 0
    if a.cmd == "apply":
        return cmd_apply(cfg)
    if a.cmd in ("rac", "tick"):
        return cmd_rac(cfg)
    if a.cmd == "probe":
        ps = probe_tick(cfg, force=a.now)
        print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in ps.items() if k != "history"}, indent=1))
        return 0
    return cmd_status(cfg, getattr(a, "json", False))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
